#: ../../library/imu.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`imu` --- IMU helper for the Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense"
msgstr ":mod:`imu` --- IMU-hjälpmodul för Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense"

#: ../../library/imu.rst:10
msgid ""
"This page documents the Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense's Python ``imu`` module (a"
" small wrapper around the on-board IMU drivers). For the OpenMV C-level "
"``imu`` module that ships on the OPENMV_N6, OPENMV_RT1060, and OPENMV_AE3 "
"camera boards, see :doc:`omv.imu`."
msgstr ""
"Den här sidan dokumenterar Python-modulen ``imu`` för Arduino Nano 33 BLE "
"Sense (ett litet omslag kring de inbyggda IMU-drivrutinerna). För OpenMV:s "
"C-nivåmodul ``imu`` som levereras med kameramodellerna OPENMV_N6, "
"OPENMV_RT1060 och OPENMV_AE3, se :doc:`omv.imu`\\ ."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:15
msgid ""
"This module is a thin board-specific wrapper that exposes the on-board "
"inertial measurement unit of the Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense as a single "
":py:class:`~imu.IMU` object. Both hardware revisions of the board are "
"handled transparently:"
msgstr ""
"Den här modulen är ett tunt kortspecifikt omslag som exponerar den inbyggda "
"tröghetsmätningsenheten (IMU) på Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense som ett enda "
":py:class:`~imu.IMU`\\ -objekt. Båda hårdvarurevisionerna av kortet hanteras"
" transparent:"

#: ../../library/imu.rst:20
msgid "**Rev 1** uses a single LSM9DS1 9-axis IMU."
msgstr "**Rev 1** använder en enda LSM9DS1 9-axlig IMU."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:21
msgid ""
"**Rev 2** combines a Bosch BMI270 (accelerometer + gyroscope) with a Bosch "
"BMM150 magnetometer."
msgstr ""
"**Rev 2** kombinerar en Bosch BMI270 (accelerometer + gyroskop) med en Bosch"
" BMM150-magnetometer."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:24
msgid ""
"The constructor probes the I2C bus for the BMI270 address (``0x68``) and "
"selects the matching driver automatically, so user code can be written once "
"and run on either revision."
msgstr ""
"Konstruktorn söker på I2C-bussen efter BMI270-adressen (\\ ``0x68``\\ ) och "
"väljer den matchande drivrutinen automatiskt, så att användarkod kan skrivas"
" en gång och köras på båda revisionerna."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:28
msgid "Example::"
msgstr "Exempel::"

#: ../../library/imu.rst:45
msgid "class IMU"
msgstr "class IMU"

#: ../../library/imu.rst:49
msgid "Construct an IMU object bound to an I2C bus."
msgstr "Konstruera ett IMU-objekt bundet till en I2C-buss."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:51
msgid ""
"*bus* is an initialised :py:class:`machine.I2C` instance connected to the "
"on-board IMU(s)."
msgstr ""
"*bus* är en initierad :py:class:`machine.I2C`\\ -instans ansluten till de "
"inbyggda IMU-enheterna."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:54
msgid ""
"On construction the bus is scanned: if a device responds at address ``0x68``"
" a `BMI270` plus `BMM150` pair is instantiated (Nano 33 BLE Sense Rev 2), "
"otherwise an `LSM9DS1` is instantiated (Rev 1). The underlying driver is "
"kept on the ``imu`` attribute and configured with default ranges and output "
"data rates."
msgstr ""
"Vid konstruktion skannas bussen: om en enhet svarar på adressen ``0x68`` "
"instansieras ett par bestående av `BMI270` och `BMM150` (Nano 33 BLE Sense "
"Rev 2), annars instansieras en `LSM9DS1` (Rev 1). Den underliggande "
"drivrutinen behålls i attributet ``imu`` och konfigureras med standardomfång"
" och utdatahastigheter."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:62
msgid ""
"Return the latest accelerometer reading as an ``(x, y, z)`` tuple in units "
"of *g* (standard gravities)."
msgstr ""
"Returnera den senaste accelerometeravläsningen som en ``(x, y, z)``\\ -tupel"
" i enheten *g* (standardtyngdaccelerationer)."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:67
msgid ""
"Return the latest gyroscope reading as an ``(x, y, z)`` tuple in degrees per"
" second."
msgstr ""
"Returnera den senaste gyroskopavläsningen som en ``(x, y, z)``\\ -tupel i "
"grader per sekund."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:72
msgid ""
"Return the latest magnetometer reading as an ``(x, y, z)`` tuple in micro-"
"tesla (uT)."
msgstr ""
"Returnera den senaste magnetometeravläsningen som en ``(x, y, z)``\\ -tupel "
"i mikrotesla (uT)."
